    summary: "Stony Brook Cancer Center says it is the overarching name for all cancer-related care, and all basic and translational research, at Stony Brook Medicine. Its mission statement is to reduce cancer-related suffering through multidisciplinary care close to home, innovative research, education and community partnership with underserved populations. Care teams typically include a surgeon, a medical oncologist, a radiation oncologist, a nurse and a social worker. The centre lists more than 100 active cancer clinical trials, offers second opinions, and runs an Office for Community Outreach and Engagement for Suffolk and Nassau counties. Its Stony Brook campus is on Lauterbur Drive, and the Phillips Family Cancer Center in Southampton, New York, is described as fully integrated with it.",
    programs: ["Multidisciplinary cancer care teams", "Clinical trials (more than 100 active cancer trials)", "Second opinions", "Cancer screening", "Office for Community Outreach and Engagement for Suffolk and Nassau counties", "Cancer services on the East End at the Phillips Family Cancer Center", "Education and training programmes, including medical physics and radiation oncology residencies"],
