    summary: "TGH Cancer Institute is the cancer institute of Tampa General Hospital. The hospital says its affiliation with the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine combines clinical care, teaching, research and advanced technologies. Its page lists twelve disease centres, from breast and colorectal and GI to sarcoma and skin cancer, and programmes including adolescent and young adult cancer, bone marrow transplant and cell therapies, cancer genetics and a precision medicine biorepository. It says the hospital is accredited by the Commission on Cancer of the American College of Surgeons, and that dedicated care navigators support patients and families. It also names partnerships with the Cancer Center of South Florida and the Lakeland Regional Health Hollis Cancer Center. New patients can call (813) 844-7585.",
    programs: ["Breast, Colorectal and GI, Early Detection and High-Risk, Esophageal, Genitourinary, Gynecologic, Head and Neck, Hematology, Lung, Neurological and Skin cancer centres, and a Sarcoma Center of Excellence", "Adolescent and Young Adult (AYA) Cancer Program", "Bone Marrow Transplant and Cell Therapies Program", "Cancer Genetics Program", "Hepatobiliary Cancer Program", "Pancreatic Cancer Program", "Precision Medicine Biorepository", "Care navigators for patients and families"],
