    summary: "UMass Memorial Health offers cancer care at UMass Memorial Medical Center in Worcester and at other sites in Central Massachusetts. Its page says several programmes are accredited by the American College of Surgeons Commission on Cancer, and that it is a member of the Association of American Cancer Institutes. Teams include imaging specialists, pathologists, surgeons, medical oncologists and radiation oncologists, and a nurse navigator coordinates appointments. It says UMass Memorial Medical Center was the first academic medical centre to join the Dana-Farber Cancer Institute's Cancer Care Collaborative. Services named include low-dose CT lung screening, a High-Risk Breast Cancer Clinic, genetic testing, palliative care, a Cancer Survivorship Program and paediatric cancer care at Children's Medical Center. Research and trials are run in partnership with UMass Chan Medical School.",
    programs: ["Low-dose CT lung cancer screening", "High-Risk Breast Cancer Clinic", "Cancer genetic testing", "Cancer research and clinical trials with UMass Chan Medical School", "Palliative care", "Cancer Survivorship Program", "Paediatric haematology and cancer care", "Nurse navigator coordination"],
