    summary: "The WVU Cancer Institute states its mission as overcoming the unique cancer challenges facing West Virginians by transforming cancer outcomes through integrated patient care, cancer research and education. Its vision is the elimination of cancer outcome disparities and an improved health trajectory for West Virginians and fellow Appalachians. Its radiation oncology department is accredited by the American College of Radiology, and its cellular therapy programme holds Foundation for the Accreditation of Cellular Therapy accreditation for blood and marrow transplant and for immune effector cell therapy. Its Comprehensive Breast Care Program holds National Accreditation Program for Breast Centers accreditation. The Mary Babb Randolph Cancer Center is named on its accreditations page as part of the institute.",
